//covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7843840-L.jpg","cover":"","coverMode":"external","r":0,"rSrc":"","baseRatings":0,"baseReviews":0,"pop":0,"st":"مستوردة","ch":0,"vol":0,"pages":0,"sc":{},"prog":{"ch":0},"mySt":null,"synopsis":"In this graphic memoir, Harrison documents through comic illustration and short personal essays what it means to live with breast cancer. She confronts with heartbreaking honesty the crises of identity that cancer brings. She struggles to reconcile her long-term goals with an uncertain future, balancing the innate sadness of cancer with everyday acts of hope and wonder. She also examines those quiet moments of helplessness and loving with her husband, her family, and her friends, while they all adjust to the new normal.","genres":["Patients","Cancer in women","Breast","Biography","Cancer","Comics & graphic novels, nonfiction, biography & memoir","Cancer, patients, biography","New York Times reviewed","Comic books, strips","Health","Bandes dessinées","Santé","Breast Neoplasms","Personal narratives","Essays","Sein","Biographies","Patientes"],"pl":"Open Library","_apiSource":"Open Library","_apiSourceId":"OL17571223W","provenance":{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17571223W","method":"monthly-work-dump","publicationCutoff":null,"aiScreening":"declared-tags-only"},"_catalogIdentityKey":"comics|in between days"},{"id":"ol-OL17732983W","title":"Elephant man","ar":"Elephant man","auth":"Greg Houston","authorKeys":["/authors/OL6786887A"],"authorAliases":[],"type":"كوميكس","yr":0,"sourceCoverUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8011675-L.jpg","cover":"","coverMode":"external","r":0,"rSrc":"","baseRatings":0,"baseReviews":0,"pop":0,"st":"مستوردة","ch":0,"vol":0,"pages":0,"sc":{},"prog":{"ch":0},"mySt":null,"synopsis":"\"Baltimore has a great hero. He's always there just when he's needed to thwart crime! This marvel is Elephant Man. Yes, none other than the deformed and hideous man himself! But such power and the adulation that follows it begets much jealousy. Before you know it, one of the city's best known TV anchors, 'handsome' Dick Denton and another hideous being fused by some radioactive accident: the Priest, The Rabbi and The Duck, come together to seek his demise and ridicule him in public! Will Elephant Man overcome this new challenge?\"--P. [4] of cover.","genres":["Proteus syndrome","Patients","Comic books, strips","Comics & graphic novels, superheroes"],"pl":"Open Library","_apiSource":"Open Library","_apiSourceId":"OL17732983W","provenance":{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17732983W","method":"monthly-work-dump","publicationCutoff":null,"aiScreening":"declared-tags-only"},"_catalogIdentityKey":"comics|elephant man"},{"id":"ol-OL17900319W","title":"Big star Otto","ar":"Big star Otto","auth":"Bill Slavin","authorKeys":["/authors/OL832393A"],"authorAliases":[],"type":"كوميكس","yr":0,"sourceCoverUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8215703-L.jpg","cover":"","coverMode":"external","r":0,"rSrc":"","baseRatings":0,"baseReviews":0,"pop":0,"st":"مستوردة","ch":0,"vol":0,"pages":0,"sc":{},"prog":{"ch":0},"mySt":null,"synopsis":"\"In this conclusion to the Elephants Never Forget graphic novel trilogy, big-hearted hero Otto and his parrot pal Crackers have landed in Hollywood, the final stop in their journey across America in search of their good friend Georgie the chimpanzee. They've been hot on Georgie's trail since he was abducted from Africa by the sinister Man with the Wooden Nose, and now they're sure they've finally found his location. Reaching him is going to be tough, however, with a dishonest acting agent, a shadowy villain, disgruntled wannabe animal actors and some elephant-rights activists, among others, regularly thwarting their plans. It seems that greed and the quest for fame \"can do awful things to folk\" here in Tinseltown, as a wise old elephant tells Otto. Can true friendship possibly win in the end? This is an immensely entertaining adventure story, with fantastic artwork by award-winning illustrator Bill Slavin that is detailed, energetic and packed with visual humor throughout. It's a perfect fit for emerging and reluctant readers looking for a strong visual narrative to help them through a book. The hilarious storyline offers lots of sly, clever jokes driven by high-velocity action and a heartwarming and lovable main character. In fact, what helps set the books in this series apart is that, through all of the misadventures that get in his way, Otto's good nature and generosity remain constant, and his commitment to finding his friend never wavers, providing wonderful character education lessons on friendship, perseverance and teamwork\"--","genres":["Animals","Elephants","Juvenile fiction","Graphic novels","Fiction","Adventure graphic novels","Parrots","Comic books, strips","Friendship","Cartoons and comics","Adventure and adventurers","Children's fiction"],"pl":"Open Library","_apiSource":"Open Library","_apiSourceId":"OL17900319W","provenance":{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17900319W","method":"monthly-work-dump","publicationCutoff":null,"aiScreening":"declared-tags-only"},"_catalogIdentityKey":"comics|big star otto"},{"id":"ol-OL18006751W","title":"Strip Search","ar":"Strip Search","auth":"Stephanie Bennett","authorKeys":["/authors/OL5347294A"],"authorAliases":[],"type":"كوميكس","yr":0,"sourceCoverUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/636728-L.jpg","cover":"","coverMode":"external","r":0,"rSrc":"","baseRatings":0,"baseReviews":0,"pop":0,"st":"مستوردة","ch":0,"vol":0,"pages":0,"sc":{},"prog":{"ch":0},"mySt":null,"synopsis":"","genres":["Comic books, strips","Humor, form, comic strips & cartoons"],"pl":"Open Library","_apiSource":"Open Library","_apiSourceId":"OL18006751W","provenance":{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18006751W","method":"monthly-work-dump","publicationCutoff":null,"aiScreening":"declared-tags-only"},"_catalogIdentityKey":"comics|strip search"},{"id":"ol-OL18787829W","title":"William Shakespeare